    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5501A\n\nSPONSOR: OBERACKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending authorization to\nimpose certain taxes in the county of Sullivan\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize Sullivan County to continue to impose a total additional\n1.00% county sales tax rate for an additional two years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends clause 33 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph\nof section 1210 of the Tax Law to authorize Sullivan County to impose an\nadditional county sales tax rate of one percent until November 13, 2025.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSullivan County has requested authorization to extend the authority to\nimpose an additional one percent sales and compensating use tax. The\nrevenue anticipated from this additional tax will allow the County of\nSullivan to continue to provide services deemed vital to the community,\nwhile maintaining a balanced budget.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nAdditional county sales and compensating use tax rate of one percent\nextended through November 30,2023 by Chapter 58 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
